     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""coverloop — evidence gate for AI-written changes.
     3	
     4	Subcommands:
     5	  init    scaffold .coverloop/ (config + reports dir) in the current repo
     6	  attest  record evidence (test run, reviewer verdicts, human approval)
     7	          into a report bound to the current HEAD commit
     8	  gate    verify the required evidence exists for the given risk tier;
     9	          exit 0 only if every required gate has a passing, HEAD-bound record
    10	
    11	Design rules (do not weaken):
    12	  * FAIL CLOSED: missing config (non-L0), missing report (non-L0), stale
    13	    evidence, unreadable JSON, unknown tier -> non-zero exit. A malformed,
    14	    forged, or SHA-mismatched report fails EVERY tier, including L0.
    15	  * The GATE never sends code anywhere and never calls a model — it only
    16	    inspects local files and git metadata. `attest` runs the project's own
    17	    test command and, when given `--codex-run` / `--glm-run`, executes those
    18	    reviewer commands and captures their hashed transcripts; `--codex-log` /
    19	    `--glm-log` instead ATTACH an existing transcript (redacted + hashed, no
    20	    re-run — source "attached", one honesty notch below "captured"); otherwise
    21	    a reviewer verdict is self-attested (a recorded claim). The verdict itself
    22	    is always caller-stated (reviewer output is prose, not a status).
    23	    `gate --require-transcript` makes L2/L3 reject self-attested reviewer
    24	    verdicts and demand a committed transcript (captured or attached);
    25	    `--require-executed` is stricter (executed capture only).
    26	  * Evidence binds to a commit SHA. The gate accepts a report bound to an
    27	    ancestor commit ONLY when the diff from that ancestor to HEAD touches
    28	    nothing but files under .coverloop/reports/ — this makes the
    29	    "attest, then commit the report" flow possible while guaranteeing any
    30	    CODE change after attestation still invalidates the evidence.
    31	
    32	Honest threat model: this verifies that evidence EXISTS and is bound to
    33	the commit under review; it cannot stop someone from hand-writing a lying
    34	report. It turns silent drift into an explicit, committed, auditable lie —
    35	and in CI the report travels with the PR, where a reviewer can see it.
