  1026	    first (codex exec / glm-review in the terminal), so `--codex-run` would
  1027	    mean paying for the SAME review twice — and in practice evidence stays
  1028	    self-attested. An attached transcript is one honesty notch below captured
  1029	    (the tool didn't execute the command, so there's no exit-code/execution
  1030	    binding) but far above a bare claim: the transcript is committed, readable
  1031	    in the PR, and hash-bound to this commit like any captured log.
  1032	    """
  1033	    if os.path.islink(src_path):
  1034	        fail_usage(f"--{name}-log: {src_path} is a symlink — pass the real transcript file")
  1035	    if not os.path.isfile(src_path):
  1036	        fail_usage(f"--{name}-log: no such file: {src_path}")
  1037	    # Refuse sources inside the reports dir: attaching the gate's own artifacts
  1038	    # would launder a withheld failed-run log, or replay an OLD commit's log,
  1039	    # into fresh "attached" evidence with one command. (Replaying a copy made
  1040	    # elsewhere is the documented attester's-word ceiling — but the tool must
  1041	    # not accept its own rejection/stale artifacts as new evidence.)
  1042	    src_real = os.path.realpath(src_path)
  1043	    reports_real = os.path.join(os.path.realpath(root), REPORTS_DIR)
  1044	    inside_reports = src_real == reports_real or src_real.startswith(reports_real + os.sep)
