  2377	    """(command, readable) for the version of test_command BEFORE the most
  2378	    recent commit that touched the gate config.
  2379	
  2380	    Read from the config file's own git history rather than from reports or
  2381	    from the evidence baseline, because both of those vanish in exactly the
  2382	    case this exists to catch: rewriting test_command invalidates the ancestor
  2383	    evidence (the recorded command must match the current one), which drops the
  2384	    baseline to the root, and a deleted report is otherwise indistinguishable
  2385	    from first-time setup.
  2386	
  2387	    A config with only ONE commit touching it was created, not changed — that is
  2388	    adoption, and a floor that fires on adoption is a floor people route around.
  2389	    `readable` is False only when git could not answer, which fails closed.
