Real defects:

- **P1 — A second config commit launders a weakened test command.** `_previous_test_command()` compares only the last two commits touching the config. Change `test_command` to `true`, then touch another config field in a subsequent commit: both observed versions contain `true`, so no L2 promotion occurs. The config remains L1 and no reviewer runs, allowing `SAFE TO MERGE`. [bin/coverloop:2391](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2391), [bin/coverloop:2497](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2497), [bin/coverloop:2585](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2585)

- **P1 — Repo-controlled tests can replace the supposedly trusted reviewer before it runs.** The configured test command executes first with the operator’s privileges; reviewer commands execute afterward. Nothing requires an external reviewer executable or its PATH directory to be immutable, and the final integrity check examines only HEAD and repository files. A malicious test can overwrite a user-owned reviewer wrapper with one printing `VERDICT: PASS`, bypassing L2/L3 independent review without dirtying the repository. [bin/coverloop:1392](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1392), [bin/coverloop:1416](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1416), [bin/coverloop:2560](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2560), [bin/coverloop:2676](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2676)

- **P1 — A lower-tier human approval survives a later L3 elevation.** `attest --approve` is allowed at every tier. Elevating an existing report updates its tier and elevation metadata without clearing `human_gate`; evaluation then accepts the old approval. Thus approval recorded before the L3 reason existed can authorize that elevation. [bin/coverloop:1352](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1352), [bin/coverloop:1435](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1435), [bin/coverloop:1718](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:1718)

- **P2 — The verdict parser accepts multiple PASS markers contrary to its protocol.** It rejects non-PASS markers but never requires exactly one marker; `VERDICT: PASS\nVERDICT: PASS` returns pass despite documentation requiring no other `VERDICT:` line. [bin/coverloop:2264](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/bin/coverloop:2264), [docs/GATE.md:61](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/protocol-loop/docs/GATE.md:61)

